# Overrides (docs/flow.md): card effects that lift the default targeting and blocking rules.
# Seating A B C D: A's prey is B, its predator D; C is neither.
# Invented cards: Long Reach (action card, bleed any Methuselah), Wide Gaze (vampire, bleeds any
# Methuselah), Hawk Watch (reaction, blocks ignoring the restrictions). Iron Ward and Quick Feed
# are untagged.
seed 5
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
seat D dave
crypt A "Vera Nightfall" *6 "Wide Gaze" *6
library A "Long Reach" *20 "Iron Ward" *20
crypt B "Tomas Grey" *12
library B "Quick Feed" *40
crypt C "Ilse Várga" *12
library C "Hawk Watch" *20 "Quick Feed" *20
crypt D "Tomas Grey" *12
library D "Quick Feed" *40
start

A> move "Vera Nightfall" ready
A> move "Wide Gaze" ready
A> draw 3
B> move B:uncontrolled:1 ready
C> move C:uncontrolled:1 ready
C> draw 3
D> move D:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> next
A> next
expect turn 1 A minion

# By default only the prey can be bled.
reject:forbidden A> bleed A:ready:1 C

# A tagged action card lets the bleed go anywhere, no claim needed.
A> bleed A:ready:1 C with "Long Reach"
log public A: Vera Nightfall bleeds C with Long Reach, ignoring the prey restriction (Long Reach)
expect impulse C
C> pass
A> resolve failure
A> unlock A:ready:1

# An untagged action card needs a claim, and is flagged as unverified.
reject:forbidden A> bleed A:ready:1 C with "Iron Ward"
A> bleed A:ready:1 C with "Iron Ward" override
log public A: Vera Nightfall bleeds C with Iron Ward, ignoring the prey restriction (Iron Ward, unverified)
C> pass
A> resolve failure
A> unlock A:ready:1

# A card in play can be the source: here a vampire whose text allows it.
A> bleed A:ready:1 D via A:ready:2
log public A: Vera Nightfall bleeds D, ignoring the prey restriction (Wide Gaze)
expect impulse D
D> pass
A> resolve failure
A> unlock A:ready:1

# The source must be public and yours.
reject:invalid A> bleed A:ready:1 C via B:ready:1

# In casual games, a claim without a card is accepted and flagged.
A> bleed A:ready:1 C override
log public A: Vera Nightfall bleeds C, ignoring the prey restriction (no card named, unverified)
C> pass
A> resolve failure
A> unlock A:ready:1

# Blocking when not eligible: C holds, then blocks with a reaction played from the hand.
A> bleed A:ready:1
expect impulse B
C> hold
B> pass
expect impulse C
reject:forbidden C> block C:ready:1
C> block C:ready:1 via "Hawk Watch"
log public C tries to block with Ilse Várga, ignoring the blocking restrictions (Hawk Watch)
expect count C:ashHeap 1
expect count C:hand 10
expect impulse A
A> pass
expect impulse C
C> pass
expect action bleed A combat
C> endcombat
expect action none
A> unlock A:ready:1

# An untagged reaction is accepted as unverified.
C> unlock C:ready:1
A> bleed A:ready:1
C> hold
B> pass
C> block C:ready:1 via "Quick Feed"
log public C tries to block with Ilse Várga, ignoring the blocking restrictions (Quick Feed, unverified)
C> unblock
expect action bleed A blocks
expect impulse A
A> pass
# C still holds. Giving up the attempt was a decision not to block: no second override.
expect impulse C
reject:forbidden C> block C:ready:1 via C:hand:1
C> pass
expect action bleed A resolution
